WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.919
Welcome to Grade 4 English, Unit 9: Places, People, and Plans.

2
00:00:04.999 --> 00:00:08.870
This unit is all about places, people, and plans.

3
00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:17.980
You will learn the words we use to talk about travelling:
the airport, the station, the museum, the capital city,

4
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.109
and much more.

5
00:00:19.189 --> 00:00:27.656
You will meet the people we find in busy places, like
the customer at a shop and the workers in an office.

6
00:00:27.736 --> 00:00:36.363
Most of all, you will learn how to make plans — how to
invite a friend, how to say what you are going to do,

7
00:00:36.443 --> 00:00:39.024
and how to give clear directions.

8
00:00:39.104 --> 00:00:43.942
By the end, you will be able to plan a whole trip in English,

9
00:00:44.022 --> 00:00:50.876
just like Amal and Noah do in this unit's
story when they explore the city of Mombasa.

10
00:00:50.956 --> 00:00:57.649
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

11
00:00:57.729 --> 00:01:06.851
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name many kinds
of places — the airport, station, museum, mall, and more.

12
00:01:06.931 --> 00:01:14.806
You will also talk about the people and movement in
busy places, using words like customer and arrive.

13
00:01:14.886 --> 00:01:19.329
You will also invite someone politely using would like to.

14
00:01:19.409 --> 00:01:22.214
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

15
00:01:22.294 --> 00:01:28.386
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
tourism, airport, station, railroad, capital, nation.

16
00:01:28.466 --> 00:01:33.436
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

17
00:01:33.516 --> 00:01:37.363
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

18
00:01:37.443 --> 00:01:42.391
The reading sequence includes A Trip to
the Capital and Living Near the Equator.

19
00:01:42.471 --> 00:01:43.271
Read actively.

20
00:01:43.351 --> 00:01:47.608
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

21
00:01:47.688 --> 00:01:51.693
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

22
00:01:51.773 --> 00:01:54.843
The first language focus is Would like to.

23
00:01:54.923 --> 00:02:01.668
“Would like to” is a polite way to say what
you want, or to invite someone to do something.

24
00:02:01.748 --> 00:02:08.493
It is a kinder, softer way of saying “I want
to”, and it keeps you friendly and respectful.

25
00:02:08.573 --> 00:02:16.668
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

26
00:02:16.748 --> 00:02:20.554
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1: Invite a Friend.

27
00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:24.967
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

28
00:02:25.047 --> 00:02:28.326
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

29
00:02:28.406 --> 00:02:31.817
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

30
00:02:31.897 --> 00:02:33.425
You are ready to begin.

31
00:02:33.505 --> 00:02:40.349
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

32
00:02:40.429 --> 00:02:43.706
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

33
00:02:43.786 --> 00:02:51.469
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
